From: beardedeagle <randy@heroictek.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat(catalog): give local models a default embedding concurrency

The indexing pipeline resolves its batch concurrency from the model's catalog entry.
Local models that do not declare defaultConcurrency fall back to a hardcoded single
worker, so an index job embeds one file at a time even though local embeddings
parallelize fine. Only the model2vec potion-* entries declare it today.

Give every local llama-cpp and transformers-js model a default of 2, matching the
existing potion-* entries. Two contexts measured fastest on an M-series host: eight
peaked near 11 GB and ran slower, while two ran at 3.75 GB.

 src/engine/models/catalog.ts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/engine/models/catalog.ts b/src/engine/models/catalog.ts
index 9e035e6..46daaff 100644
--- a/src/engine/models/catalog.ts
+++ b/src/engine/models/catalog.ts
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ export const EMBEDDING_MODEL_CATALOG = {
     format: "embeddinggemma",
     contextSize: 2048,
     maxBatchSize: 16,
+    defaultConcurrency: 2,
   },
 
   "local/qwen3-embedding-0.6b": {
@@ -66,6 +67,7 @@ export const EMBEDDING_MODEL_CATALOG = {
